Crumb for Debian
================

The Debian build preserves Crumb's normal shell, supervised agent runtime,
Pollinations integration, local sessions, and bundled marketplace catalogue.
It is built entirely from Debian-provided Rust crates and links to the system
SQLite library.

Native desktop keyring support and remote Sigstore marketplace verification
are not enabled in this build because their Rust dependency families are not
yet present in Debian. Provider credentials can instead be supplied through
the documented environment variables. A request that requires the unavailable
native credential store or Sigstore verifier fails explicitly; it never falls
back to unverified remote installation.

The feature difference is tracked in the upstream Debian packaging document:
https://github.com/elixpo/crumb.elixpo/blob/main/docs/development/debian-packaging.md
